    "interpretation": "Exploratory seed-0 six-run study with two fixed configurations selected using the v0 primary score: M=1 with H2/L1 and M=3 with H4/L2. Both use predicted mean commands for executor training and inference. Low actor loss backpropagates through the predicted commands into the planner; actor losses do not update goal_rep, which learns only from value loss. Offline action labels and low-actor AWR remain dataset-based. High-actor beta is 0.5, 1.0 or 2.0, while low_alpha remains 3. All other v0 training/evaluation settings are retained: final-only full-BPTT per-waypoint cumulative AWR, external K=1, Delta=50, latent width 128 and Mixer intermediate width 32. No adjacent-difference weighting or intermediate/deep supervision is introduced. The two shared modifications are bundled, so this study does not identify their separate effects. Scores use exactly 800k/900k/1M; three checkpoints are not independent seeds. Execution requested on physical GPU 1 with two concurrent training workers. Method names sort by beta, then pair M=1 and M=3.",
